class:: TinkerbellMap
summary:: Trigger-driven raw Tinkerbell map coordinates
categories:: UGens>Generators>Chaotic>Maps
related:: Guides/StochasticDynamicsUGens, Classes/DeJongMap

description::

Implements the polynomial Tinkerbell recurrence code::x' = x*x - y*y + a*x + b*y:: and code::y' = 2*x*y + c*x + d*y::. Both equations use the old state.

The outputs are raw state coordinates. They are not normalized audio signals and may diverge for some parameters.

Like link::Classes/Stepper::, it advances and holds on trigger edges; unlike Stepper, it evolves two polynomially coupled coordinates.

subsection:: State-space portrait

image::tinkerbell-map-phase.png#The default Tinkerbell orbit after its transient. x is horizontal and y is vertical; points retain the map's discrete-time character.::

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: trig
Advance on a rising edge.
argument:: a
Old-x linear coefficient in x.
argument:: b
Old-y linear coefficient in x.
argument:: c
Old-x linear coefficient in y.
argument:: d
Old-y linear coefficient in y.
argument:: x0
Initial x coordinate.
argument:: y0
Initial y coordinate.
argument:: reset
Restore initial coordinates on a rising edge.
Returns:: Two audio-rate outputs: x and y.

method:: kr
Control-rate version with the same arguments and outputs.

instancemethods::

examples::

code::
(
{ TinkerbellMap.ar(Impulse.ar(1000))[1] * 0.03 }.play
)
::

code::
(
{
    var state = TinkerbellMap.ar(Impulse.ar(300));
    Pan2.ar(state[0] * 0.03, state[1].tanh)
}.play
)
::

subsection:: Real-time phase portrait

code::
(
SDPhaseView.open(
    "Tinkerbell map: x-y phase portrait",
    [-1.4, 0.7], [-1.8, 0.8],
    { TinkerbellMap.kr(Impulse.kr(120)) },
    { |state|
        Pan2.ar(
            SinOsc.ar(state[0].clip(-1.4, 0.7).linexp(-1.4, 0.7, 100, 1800), 0, 0.06),
            state[1].clip(-1.8, 0.8).linlin(-1.8, 0.8, -1, 1)
        )
    }
);
)
::

